From 4a5572aeac576ebbb4aabee605d58c053bf651b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 01:52:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] StaticRecomp: tell the module which chunks are verified;
 hand it the pipe

From Piconet's RecompCore, for modules built with Piconet's DolRecomp
fork and its fastlookup.py (native_tables.c):
- PublishChunkState: through the module's staticrecomp_set_native_valid,
  each function's entry byte follows its chunk's state (verified or not)
  and its indirect-call table entry is set only when it may be called
  through the table (not with relocatable RELs, forced-fallback ranges or
  host calls in it). All cleared at load and at ClearCache; set again
  wherever a chunk's state changes (verification, invalidation, REL
  relink). Needed by DOLRECOMP_INDIRECT_CALLS=native and closed bodies.
- PublishGatherPipe / HookGatherPipeFlush: through the module's
  staticrecomp_set_gather_pipe, generated code built with
  DOLRECOMP_GATHER_PIPE=inline appends write-gather pipe stores to
  Dolphin's pipe itself and calls the flush hook at 32 bytes. Not while
  the lockstep verifier runs; SRNP_GATHER_INLINE=0 keeps the hook path.
- STATICRECOMP_DISPATCH_SAMPLES=1 prints up to 2000 dispatch sites.
A module without these symbols runs as before (both are looked up at
load and printed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
